# Bump Version on Changes

After making **substantive changes** to the eBay Bot project (code, templates, config, styling), **always increment the VERSION file** by 1.

## When to Bump

- Code changes (app.py, API routes, listing logic, etc.)
- Template changes (landing.html, app.html, etc.)
- UI/styling updates
- Feature additions or fixes

## When to Skip

- Typo fixes only
- Comments/docs only
- Purely exploratory/informational changes

## How

1. Read the current version from `VERSION` (e.g. `4.133`)
2. Increment the number by 1 (e.g. `4.134`)
3. Write the new version to `VERSION`

Do this as part of the same change set—don't leave it for later.
